-- title:
--   Hecke–Galois datum over an arbitrary complete discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   The weight-$2$ Hecke algebra $\mathbb{T}^{S}(N)=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_{2}(\Gamma_{0}(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$. The first hypothesis `hES` is a pointwise existence statement, quantified over all data: for every prime $p'$, every level $N'\ge 1$, every finite $S'\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ with $p'\in S'$ and every prime divisor of $N'$ in $S'$, every complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}'$ of characteristic zero with finite residue field and $p'\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}'}$, and every ring homomorphism $\chi:\mathbb{T}^{S'}(N')\to\mathcal{O}'$, there exist such a ring $\mathcal{O}''$, an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra structure on it which is module-finite, local and injective, and a rank-$2$ adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $\mathcal{O}''$ (a free $\mathcal{O}''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}V$ that is trivial modulo $\mathfrak{m}^n$ on some finite level for each $n$) such that for all primes $\ell\nmid N'$, $\ell\notin S'$, every valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit and every $\sigma$ acting on the residue field of $A$ as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ in the decomposition group, $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=X^{2}-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$, and $\rho$ is unramified at every prime $q\nmid N'$ with $q\neq p'$ (no element of the image of the inertia subgroup acts nontrivially). Fixing now a prime $p$, a level $N\ge 1$, a finite $S$ with $p\in S$ and all primes dividing $N$ in $S$, a complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}$ with $p\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ (neither finiteness of its residue field nor characteristic zero is assumed), a homomorphism $\theta:\mathbb{T}^{S}(N)\to k=\mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}$, a residual Galois representation $\bar\rho$ over $k$ that is absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$) and satisfies $\operatorname{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^{2}-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ at all Frobenius elements as above, a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$ that is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module with local structure map, and a homomorphism $\pi:\mathbb{T}^{S}(N)\to T$ which reduces to $\theta$ composed with $k\to T/\mathfrak{m}_T$, whose image generates $T$ as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, such that every $\mathcal{O}$-valued point $\chi$ of $\mathbb{T}^{S}(N)$ reducing to $\theta$ factors as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $T\to\mathcal{O}$ through $\pi$, and such that $\mathcal{O}\to T\to T/\mathfrak{m}_T$ is surjective: the conclusion is that there is a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N S 𝒪 θ T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) whose structure map is exactly $\pi$ and whose attached adic Galois representation over $T$ is unramified at every prime $q\nmid N$ with $q\neq p$. Unfolding the datum, this provides a rank-$2$ adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ with $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=X^{2}-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ at the Frobenius elements at all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, with absolutely irreducible residual representation.
--
--   This is the gluing step that converts the family of Galois representations attached to the individual $\mathcal{O}$-valued (and finite-extension-valued) eigensystems of a local Hecke algebra into a single representation with coefficients in that algebra, packaged as a Hecke–Galois datum; it is the form of the statement used over an arbitrary complete discrete valuation ring with $p$ in its maximal ideal, rather than only over one with finite residue field and characteristic zero. It is cited by [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_forall_isUnramifiedAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_forall_isUnramifiedAt), which supplies the Galois-theoretic input to the modularity-lifting arguments.
